1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
In an emergency, there is no time

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:06,800
to discover an exit changed—or an
assistance role has no owner.

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:09,860
Teams need to rehearse those
decisions together.

4
00:00:09,860 --> 00:00:11,500
Rehearse before conditions change.

5
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:15,200
The facilitator gets one command room
for the plan and fictional occupants,

6
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:20,340
response roles, scripted changes,
and review evidence.

7
00:00:20,340 --> 00:00:22,500
This is one real page take.

8
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:27,000
The facilitator selects Floor Seven and
advances one declared tool at a time.

9
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,460
The plan is read before
the scenario starts.

10
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:35,060
The Studio is inspected. Stair B becomes
unavailable. Exits are compared.

11
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:38,300
And the decision is recorded.

12
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:40,420
Nothing auto-completes the exercise
or contacts a building system.

13
00:00:40,420 --> 00:00:43,000
The plan changed.
The facilitator draws a path.

14
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:46,500
The page measures it, checks its endpoint
against the scenario's exit status,

15
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:50,800
and keeps the result visible without
calling it a real evacuation route.

16
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:54,680
The people layer makes
responsibility visible.

17
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:59,500
Each fictional responder has a role,
exercise position, task, and boundary.

18
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:03,100
The facilitator records
only confirmed actions.

19
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:05,060
Every call leaves a trace.

20
00:01:05,060 --> 00:01:09,200
A human request enters
the Incident Commander,

21
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:13,700
which routes to plan, people,
equipment, or review specialists.

22
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:18,240
Named page tools read or update
one deterministic state.

23
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:23,160
The interface changes,
the trace records the result, and the human
controls the final decision.

24
00:01:23,680 --> 00:01:28,720
Select any call to see its input, output,
purpose, visible page change,

25
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:34,680
duration, and guardrail. Open gaps remain
visible instead of being silently resolved.

26
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:37,500
The agent prepares.
The human decides.

27
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:39,000
When every problem has an owner, the agent
stages an after-action draft.

28
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:42,620
A Fire Safety Manager reviews
the evidence and uses the separate
human approval control.

29
00:01:43,580 --> 00:01:48,580
Five hundred shuffled workflows test
transitions, repeat-safe actions,

30
00:01:48,580 --> 00:01:49,120
route boundaries, and human approval.

31
00:01:51,340 --> 00:01:55,000
Every tool has clear limits
and visible consequences.

32
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,960
The result is a reviewable training record,
not a safety certification.

33
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:03,940
This is fictional tabletop training
software. Try the live drill.
